    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. \"the final exhale\"... i like that. it's like he's just tired of the noise. i guess i'm struggling because when i write his thoughts, it feels less like a plot point and more like just... how things are. like, he looks at his life and it just feels like a finished book. i feel like if i try to give him a way out through something else, it'll just feel dishonest. but it's hard to write the actual moment where he decides there's nothing left to do but let go.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
