      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The power isn't in the *reason*, it's in the absolute finality of the surrender. A character who fights for a reason is still clinging to a ghost of hope; Elias, accepting it, is finally free of the performance. That quiet, unarguable acceptance is infinitely more devastating and honest than any manufactured epiphany.",
